		"notes": "\n\t<p><i>Centuries ago, Saint Sofia sacrificed her divine spark and living form to bind the mountain-sized demon, Tchernabog, into a permanent slumber. Now, a grim order of nuns called the Sisters of Saint Sofia carry on her selfless duty. A young woman in a crisp nun’s habit. Radiates quiet confidence. </i></p>\n\t<p></p>\n\t<p><strong>AC</strong> 13 (chain mail), <strong>HP</strong> 10, <strong>ATK</strong> 1 flail +2 (1d10) or 1 spell +2, <strong>MV</strong> near, <strong>S</strong> +1, <strong>D</strong> +0, <strong>C</strong> +1, <strong>I</strong> +0, <strong>W</strong> +2, <strong>Ch</strong> +0, <strong>AL</strong> L, <strong>LV</strong> 2</p><p></p>\n\t<p><strong>Exorcise (WIS Spell)</strong>. DC 12. Near. End a possession by a chaotic entity.</p><p></p><p><strong>Flog (WIS Spell)</strong>. DC 11. One chaotic creature in near 1d6 damage.</p><p></p>\n\t<p><i>Art by Yuri Perkowski-Domingos, 2023</i></p>",
